symfony/mcp-bundle: complete the ServerConnection request surface

`ServerConnectionInterface` forwards the SDK client's requests, but three were
missing, so an application using the bundle could not reach them at all without
dropping down to the raw `Mcp\Client`:

  * `complete()` — argument completion (`completion/complete`), which is the
    whole point of `#[CompletionProvider]` on the server side;
  * `getProtocolVersion()` — which revision was negotiated;
  * `sendRootsListChanged()` — telling a server the client's roots moved.

Adds all three, wrapped in the same error translation as the rest.

